    {
      "id": "BH07",
      "title": "Fatigue is not malady; cure is not refreshed capacity",
      "source": "definitions-plus-interpreter",
      "content_scope": "base",
      "status": "selected-dependency-chain-source-reviewed",
      "chain": "Phost fatigue becomes zpho and dawn recovery returns xpho. Malady becomes mpho with reduced Lantern and a Nectar-5 cure requirement. A restorative bed action with enough Nectar invokes curing, which becomes fatigued zpho, not fresh Phost; later recovery is another transition.",
      "boundary": "Treatment is a functional state chain with a concrete consumer and residual aftermath. All soul maladies, contamination and bed rules are not reviewed. No source-wide offline healing assumption.",
